'''Corwin Shelvay''' was an individual whose name was etched into the wall of a cave of the [[Hidden Path]] on [[Jabiim]].<ref name="Part V">{{Kenobi|Part V}}</ref> In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{SW|url=news/future-lucasfilm-projects-revealed|text=Future Lucasfilm Projects Revealed}} states that ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' is set ten [[Standard year|years]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[19 BBY]]. Therefore, ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'', including "[[Part V]]" and the [[attack on Jabiim]], must be set in [[9 BBY]].</ref> their name was among those seen by [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] during [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader's]] [[Attack on Jabiim|raid]] of the Path's base on Jabiim.<ref name="Part V" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Corwinshelvay.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Corwin Shelvay in the ''Star Wars'' Legends continuity]]
Shelvay was introduced into the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in "[[Part V]]" of ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'', released on [[June 15]], [[2022]].<ref name="Part V" /> The [[Corwin Shelvay/Legends|character]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity in "[[Calibration Check]]," a short story in ''[[Galaxy Guide 9: Fragments from the Rim]]'', a [[1993]] supplement to [[West End Games]]' ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]''. In the Legends continuity, Shelvay is a [[Human/Legends|Human]] [[Gender/Legends|male]] [[Jedi Knight/Legends|Jedi Knight]] who joined the [[Jedi Order]] after the [[Great Jedi Purge/Legends|Great Jedi Purge]], and later joined the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic/Legends|Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="GG9">''[[Galaxy Guide 9: Fragments from the Rim]]''</ref>

In the episode guide on [[StarWars.com]], Shelvay is stated as a survivor of the Jedi Purge;<ref name="Part III Guide">{{SW|url=series/obi-wan-kenobi/part-iii-guide|text=Part III Episode Guide &#124; Obi-Wan Kenobi}}</ref> however, in the Legends continuity, he joined the order after the purge had taken place under the tutelage of Jedi Master [[Darrin Arkanian]].<ref name="GG9" />

